                        "form": "die Kant"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f1327e5b-997f-489d-ba32-934f32ce7d43",
                        "entry_id": "d559f7f0-5d4b-3857-a261-6f0bcaebda26",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Kants"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                        "entry_id": "d559f7f0-5d4b-3857-a261-6f0bcaebda26",
                        "glosses": [
                            "deutscher Familienname"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87669b8c-a0c8-47b2-8b65-b49e237ec2a6",
                                "sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                                "text": "„Frau Kant (31 Jahre alt; verheiratet) arbeitet bei einem großen Reiseveranstalter. Sie nimmt seit einem halben Jahr an der Psychodramatherapiegruppe teil, …“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f4179049-79da-435b-825b-e1b83e0075a3",
                                "sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                                "text": "„Der Begriff der Antinomie läßt sich bis zu Plutarch und Quintilian zurückverfolgen, hat aber erst bei Kant seine philosophisch relevante Ausprägung gewonnen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9168deec-3223-4ec9-a0b0-101ddb5feee9",
                                "sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                                "text": "„Ich glaubte, alles von und über Kant zu kennen, in diesem Text aber stieß ich auf eine scheinbar unbedeutende Notiz, die meine Dissertation zur Makulatur werden ließ.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "270ea84c-2855-43b3-aef0-3d2134fe9edd",
                        "source_entry_id": "d559f7f0-5d4b-3857-a261-6f0bcaebda26",
                        "source_sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                        "source_sense_description": "deutscher Familienname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kant",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cc3cccf7-16ba-357b-ba02-fcdc1499cac8",
                                        "entry_id": "d4ab6ace-a1fa-3e90-8a3e-f215591a9519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A surname from German."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cbbe9dec-ea66-3bbc-b076-cf8a53be6456",
                                        "entry_id": "d4ab6ace-a1fa-3e90-8a3e-f215591a9519",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immanuel Kant, a German philosopher."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6914fe3-64bd-4a0b-bb66-c04a48b68794",
                                                "sense_id": "cbbe9dec-ea66-3bbc-b076-cf8a53be6456",
                                                "text": "So it is natural to speak of a category of all categories, which we call CAT, the objects of which are all the categories, and the arrows of which are all the functors. This raises genuine problems. Is CAT a category in itself? Our answer here is to treat CAT as a regulative idea; that is, an inevitable way of thinking about categories and functors, but not a strictly legitimate entity. (Compare the self, the universe, and God in Kant 1781.) Of course, general category theory applies to CAT, and this category that we do not quite believe in is the single one that we investigate the most."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kant",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6d1d7fa-5412-3290-9974-1979b19df4f3",
                                        "entry_id": "156c6c35-6fd9-3b91-8f52-8fccc4f73e89",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A city in Kyrgyzstan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7d5239fe-bcf5-4959-a464-db9a013f87cc",
                        "source_entry_id": "d559f7f0-5d4b-3857-a261-6f0bcaebda26",
                        "source_sense_id": "c3e906d3-178c-3ce0-a128-d68cfdbdc0b4",
                        "source_sense_description": "deutscher Familienname",
                        "target_lang_word": "Kant",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Kant",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4b7e842-8520-3203-b99d-458239b53a4a",
                                        "entry_id": "01b62428-dc7f-34c3-a069-3160216b0364",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom de famille, surtout connu par Emmanuel Kant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6f8822a1-a812-4355-8a1a-c99dd224b12c",
                                                "sense_id": "a4b7e842-8520-3203-b99d-458239b53a4a",
                                                "text": "À travers une étude sur Kant, je me passionnai pour l’idéalisme critique qui me confirmait dans mon refus de Dieu."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e00cec92-1828-4277-b534-fc3ff835ee20",
                                                "sense_id": "a4b7e842-8520-3203-b99d-458239b53a4a",
                                                "text": "Ainsi donc, qu’il s’agisse d’allumer du feu ou de résoudre une équation, qu’il s’agisse de la pensée concrète d’un Robinson ou de la pensée abstraite d’un Kant, la pensée reste essentiellement la même dans toutes ses manifestations : […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
